<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Directorate of Ukraine</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1918–1920</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Directorate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> was the collective revolutionary government of the Ukrainian People's Republic, formed in November 1918 to overthrow <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hetman">Hetman</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pavlo-skoropadsky">Pavlo Skoropadsky</a>'s German-backed Ukrainian State. Led first by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volodymyr-vynnychenko">Volodymyr Vynnychenko</a> and from 1919 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/symon-petliura">Symon Petliura</a>, it took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a> in December 1918 and restored the republic, but it lost the capital to the Bolsheviks in 1919 and was driven into exile by 1920.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/directorate-of-ukraine.jpg" alt="Directorate of Ukraine" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rz%C4%85d_URL_1920.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
